{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions","id":1131406,"title":"Clash of Wills Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-19T13:15:09-07:00","id":1131406,"title":"Clash of Wills Questions","content":"Clash of Wills is a really cool mechanic, and one that comes up a lot in our Mage games. There are a couple of areas I'm not particularly clear on, though.<br /> <br /> 1) Is the DP for a Clash of Wills determined at the time of the Clash, or when the power is activated? If a novice of Prime casts a particularly long lasting enchantment, which persists until he becomes a Master, at which point someone attempts to dispel it, does he Clash with the dice pool he had when he used the spell (say, Prime \u2022) or with his new Arcana rating as a Master?<br /> <br /> 2) Spirits Clash with Rank + Influence. Is that just their Rank plus their highest Influence, or does it have to be an Influence that's relevant to the Clash? If the latter, and there is no relevant Influence for the powers that are colliding, do they Clash with Rank alone?<br /> <br /> 3) Can you choose not to Clash?<br /> <br /> 4) Is it possible to Clash with yourself? The obvious answer is no, but it's worth asking, I think. An example of a circumstance where this might happen - you place a Prime shielding spell on yourself to help defend against hostile magic, but then also want to cast other spells on yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:28:46-07:00","id":1131417,"title":"","content":"1) Depends on wether he relinquished the spell in the meantime or not. The moment you relinquish the spell you lock its dicepool in place, but if the mage keeps control of the spell and increases his stats he should use his improved dicepool.<br /> <br /> 2) Not sure. I think it's actually the latter... Spirits really really suck at clashes of will RAW.<br /> <br /> 3) I think you can choose to fail your roll, yes.<br /> <br /> 4) You can choose to fail your own roll clashing with your spell.... but if you relinquish the protection spell you cannot choose to automatically fail the clash and would have to roll like any other mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:35:17-07:00","id":1131423,"title":"","content":"Source for not being able to backdoor your own relinquished spells or for their dice pools not improving in CoW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:40:00-07:00","id":1131428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions?p=1131423#post1131423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source for not being able to backdoor your own relinquished spells or for their dice pools not improving in CoW?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core does reference relinquished spells functioning 'as if cast by another mage', but as far as I know there are no explicit answers to this one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:16:19-07:00","id":1131466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions?p=1131428#post1131428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core does reference relinquished spells functioning 'as if cast by another mage', but as far as I know there are no explicit answers to this one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the spell functioning as cast by another mage is pretty clear. Your spells will clash against those cast by other mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:05:32-07:00","id":1131518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions?p=1131423#post1131423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Source for not being able to backdoor your own relinquished spells or for their dice pools not improving in CoW?</div> </div> </div> </div>The others awnsered the first part allready, for the second part I have no official source but it seems pretty obvious to me. When you relinquish a spell, you cut your ties to it so to speak and it becomes an entity of its own, fully distinct from the mage. Note that sympathy for example states that there is a connection between a mage and her spells, I could see relinquishing a spell cutting that sympathy aswell. Anyway back to the question : When you relinquish the spell you cut it off from yourself and the spell becomes locked in place. It seems reasonable to assume that the dicepool of the spell gets locked aswell. An unsafely relinquished spell that mutated should however be able to change its dicepool due to mutation, as could a spell cast with the practice of dynamics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T23:17:53-07:00","id":1131637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions#post1131406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2) Spirits Clash with Rank + Influence. Is that just their Rank plus their highest Influence, or does it have to be an Influence that's relevant to the Clash? If the latter, and there is no relevant Influence for the powers that are colliding, do they Clash with Rank alone?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where are the spirit clash rules? do they really get rank + influence? All i could find in m2e was &quot;Annihilate spirit&quot; which gives &quot;power + finesse&quot; to clash. Are they in Werewolf?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T00:31:25-07:00","id":1131646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131406-clash-of-wills-questions?p=1131637#post1131637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are the spirit clash rules? do they really get rank + influence? All i could find in m2e was &quot;Annihilate spirit&quot; which gives &quot;power + finesse&quot; to clash. Are they in Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave provided this info in the Simple Question thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:32:50-07:00","id":1131749,"title":"","content":"According to Werewolf (2e, p. 115):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A spirit in a Clash of Wills uses its Rank as its dice pool. If the Clash comes from the spirit using an Influence, it adds its dots in that Influence to the dice pool. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}